  {
   "id": 38,
   "plugin": "Core",
   "model": "Notes",
   "version": "2.6.6",
   "params": [],
   "pos": [
    80,
    2
   ],
   "data": {
    "text": "HEMIOLA AUDIO: MINIMAL TECHNO, 131 BPM\n\nCycle Clock 1 (131 BPM, Tintal = 16 beats, 4 bars of 4) is the master. Its BEAT gate plays the kick. Its SECTION trigger (once a bar) resets the three sequencers so they always restart on the downbeat.\nR&T 1 = sixteenths (closed hats, bass clock, and the clock for Cycle Clock 3). R&T 2 = eighths (open-hat sequencer clock, delay clock).\nCycle Clock 2 counts beats in a cycle of 2, and restarts with Cycle Clock 1 every 16 beats. Its END trigger lands on beats 2 and 4: the clap.\nCycle Clock 3 counts R&T 1's sixteenths in a cycle of 3. Its CYCLE trigger fires a stab every dotted eighth, which drifts against the bar (a hemiola). It also steps the chord sequencer.\n\nTry: change R&T 1 DIVISION to 3 or 6 for a swung or triplet feel. Change Cycle Clock 3 CYCLE to 5 or 7. Switch a mute on the Mutes module for breakdowns. Edit the gate buttons on the sequencers. Change Cycle Clock 1 CYCLE to 7 (2+2+3) for a broken-beat variation.\nTip: the first bar after loading settles, the groove locks from bar 2."
   }
  }
 ],
